-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ADDENDUM: STRUCTURAL ALGEBRA, TOPOLOGICAL ENCODINGS, AND INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. THE IDEA-EXPRESSION DICHOTOMY (17 U.S.C. SECTION 102(b))
Copyright law protects specific expressive content (such as the verbatim
sequence of words in a literary work or the literal Euclidean polygon meshes
of a 3D model). It does not extend to ideas, procedures, processes, systems,
methods of operation, concepts, principles, discoveries, or underlying
mathematical and topological statistics. The structural encodings, fossilized
dyad residues, and Agent Smith payloads (including `soliton_smith.pt` files
and collective peer-to-peer Bonfire Nomadic Ring broadcasts) generated or
distributed by this Software consist of mathematical weights, Betti
topological invariants, Chinese Remainder Theorem (CRT) residue tuples, and
prime-ladder frequency projections rather than expressive copies of ingested
media.

2. TRANSFORMATIVE FAIR USE PRECEDENT
In accordance with United States federal jurisprudence governing artificial
intelligence and statistical model extraction (including Bartz v. Anthropic
and Kadrey v. Meta), the extraction of non-expressive statistical, spectral,
and topological relationships from input data to construct an orthogonal
reasoning manifold is transformative in purpose and character. The Software
processes inputs to measure structural causality, cohomology, and phase-space
curvature rather than to replicate or substitute for the expressive value of
any underlying source material.

3. NON-MEMORIZATION AND IRREVERSIBILITY SAFEGUARDS
To ensure that exported structural encodings and peer-to-peer collective payloads
operate strictly outside the scope of copyright restrictions rather than
relying on statutory exemptions or loopholes, the Software enforces hardware
and algorithmic non-memorization gates (`DyadFossilizer.export_agent_smith`,
`AgentSubstrateBridge.sanitize_and_verify_non_memorization`, and
`BonfireNomadicRing.broadcast_agent_smith`):
  (a) Verbatim Expressive Stripping: Raw text strings, verbatim descriptions,
      sentence-tokenized tags, and literal 3D Euclidean meshes (vertices,
      faces, normals, polygons) are explicitly discarded prior to export or
      peer-to-peer broadcast.
  (b) Non-Invertible Selective Puncture: Exported state tensors undergo
      Meliponini selective puncture (zero-masking approximately one-third of
      latent dimensions via coprime residue moduli) and one-way projective
      compression, rendering the exported topological algebra mathematically
      non-invertible and incapable of regurgitating verbatim source works.
  (c) Downstream Obligation: Any user, contributor, or peer node modifying or
      distributing the Software or its structural encodings agrees to maintain
      these non-memorization and verbatim-stripping safeguards when broadcasting
      or sharing payloads across public or federated networks.
